    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0141" n="123" xml:id="pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/4–146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-01T20:00:00-04:00">April 1, 1946—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 1—6:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>923. ReEmbtel 829, Mar. 22.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d90-f1"/> Reports received from
                    Brazil indicate that profitable clandestine trade hinders Braz’s concurrence to
                    proposed natural rubber shipments. Problem is increasingly difficult for Embassy
                    since first quarter has passed with no announcement yet given re allocation for
                    either first or second quarter. Believe it imperative that immediate concurrence
                    of Braz be obtained or that tripartite agreement be officially abandoned to
                    permit thereby action by US in supplying Argentina’s essential natural rubber
                    requirements.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Rio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
